# Photography

Use a photograph when it matters what a real thing looks like. A photograph shows the actual object in the actual home, so people can recognise it when they go to find it.

## When to use a photograph

Use a photograph to show something as it really is. For example:

- the stopcock under the kitchen sink, beside the leak sensor card, so anyone at home can find it quickly
- the reset button on the boiler, beside the heating card, so a guest can restart it
- which of 2 similar white plugs in the loft is the smart plug for the dehumidifier

Take the photograph yourself, in your own home. Crop it to the part that matters and keep the file small, so it loads quickly on a wall panel and on a phone. [File formats and exporting](illustration-formats.html) explains which format to use for a photograph and where to put the file so Home Assistant can show it.

Choose the card by what the photograph is for. [Alt text](images-alt-text.html) explains what each card lets you do with alt text.

| Card | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| Picture | One photograph, from a file with `image` or from an image or person entity with `image_entity` |
| Picture entity | A photograph or camera view tied to one entity, with its name and state underneath |
| Tile, with `show_entity_picture: true` | An entity picture, such as a person’s photo, in place of the icon |

If the card cannot carry alt text, write what the photograph shows in text on the card or next to it. For example, under a photograph of the stopcock, write “Stopcock: at the back of the cupboard under the kitchen sink, to the left of the waste pipe”.

Do not add words to a photograph. Put them in text next to it. [Avoid images that contain text](images-text.html) explains why.

## When not to use a photograph

Do not use a photograph to show an idea or a feeling. A sunset does not explain an “Evening” scene, and a cosy sofa does not explain the heating schedule. Use a clear name, such as “Evening lights”, instead.

Do not use stock photographs. A picture of someone else’s thermostat shows the wrong buttons and the wrong display, which can send people to the wrong control.

## Camera images

Show a camera image only where someone needs to check a place, such as the front door when the doorbell rings. Put the camera name and the time of the picture in text next to it.

A camera image is not a photograph you chose. It shows whatever is in front of the camera, including people who did not agree to be on a shared screen. [Cameras, streams and snapshots](../home-assistant/cameras.html) owns camera states, snapshots, capture times and privacy.
